      </TableHeader>
      <TableBody>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>apiVersion</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>APIVersion defines the versioned schema of this representation of an object. Servers should convert recognized schemas to the latest internal value, and may reject unrecognized values. More info: https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#resources</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>dockerImageConfig</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>dockerImageConfig is a JSON blob that the runtime uses to set up the container. This is a part of manifest schema v2. Will not be set when the image represents a manifest list.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>dockerImageLayers</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>array</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>dockerImageLayers represents the layers in the image. May not be set if the image does not define that data or if the image represents a manifest list.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>dockerImageLayers[]</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>ImageLayer represents a single layer of the image. Some images may have multiple layers. Some may have none.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>dockerImageManifest</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>dockerImageManifest is the raw JSON of the manifest</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
